irections against her own map twice. Before following him, she asked another worker whether the path was safe.\n\nHow does the person most likely feel?","options":["trusting","doubtful","amused","grateful"],"correctAnswer":"doubtful","explanation":"The behaviour supports doubtful: she checked his directions with another worker.","difficulty":"medium","questionType":"multiple_choice","points":1,"timeLimit":120,"language":"en","eligibleGrades":[8],"tags":["ESL8-L04","ESL","2026 support sequence","lesson-check","bridge","core"],"taxonomies":[{"primarySkillCode":"eng.reading.inference","atomicSubskillCode":"eng.reading.inference.attitude-feeling","evidenceFocusCode":"eng.reading.inference.attitude-feeling.focus.esl-feeling-from-clues","assessmentProcessCode":"BH-AO3","cognitiveProcess":"analyze","evidenceStatement":"Infer a person's likely attitude or feeling using behavioural clues in a self-contained short text. In this item, the correct response is: doubtful"}]},{"externalId":"esl-path-20261013-g8-l04-02","topic":"ESL8-L04 · Infer feelings from clues","questionText":"Read:\nDani checked the new guide's directions against her own map twice. Before following him, she asked another worker whether the path was safe.\n\nWhich clue best supports the idea that the person feels doubtful?","options":["she thanked him without checking","she followed him immediately","she checked his directions with another worker","she lost her map"],"correctAnswer":"she checked his directions with another worker","explanation":"This clue directly supports the feeling of being doubtful.","difficulty":"medium","questionType":"multiple_choice","points":1,"timeLimit":120,"language":"en","eligibleGrades":[8],"tags":["ESL8-L04","ESL","2026 support sequence","lesson-check","bridge","core"],"taxonomies":[{"primarySkillCode":"eng.reading.inference","atomicSubskillCode":"eng.reading.inference.attitude-feeling","evidenceFocusCode":"eng.reading.inference.attitude-feeling.focus.esl-feeling-evidence","asse