 feelings from clues","questionText":"Read:\nTim expected his team to win. After the final score appeared, he lowered his head and put the team flag away without speaking.\n\nWhich clue best supports the idea that the person feels disappointed?","options":["he lowered his head after seeing the score","he cheered at the score","he raised the flag proudly","he sang to celebrate"],"correctAnswer":"he lowered his head after seeing the score","explanation":"This clue directly supports the feeling of being disappointed.","difficulty":"medium","questionType":"multiple_choice","points":1,"timeLimit":120,"language":"en","eligibleGrades":[8],"tags":["ESL8-L04","ESL","2026 support sequence","fresh-recheck","bridge","core"],"taxonomies":[{"primarySkillCode":"eng.reading.inference","atomicSubskillCode":"eng.reading.inference.attitude-feeling","evidenceFocusCode":"eng.reading.inference.attitude-feeling.focus.esl-feeling-evidence","assessmentProcessCode":"BH-AO3","cognitiveProcess":"analyze","evidenceStatement":"Select a textual clue that supports the stated inference about a person's feeling. In this item, the correct response is: he lowered his head after seeing the score"}]},{"externalId":"esl-path-20261013-g8-l04-09","topic":"ESL8-L04 · Infer feelings from clues","questionText":"Read:\nZara thanked the class for helping her finish the project. 'I could not have done this without you,' she said, handing them small cards.\n\nHow does the person most likely feel?","options":["suspicious","grateful","angry","jealous"],"correctAnswer":"grateful","explanation":"The behaviour supports grateful: she thanked the class for their help.","difficulty":"medium","questionType":"multiple_choice","points":1,"timeLimit":120,"language":"en","eligibleGrades":[8],"tags":["ESL8-L04","ESL","2026 support sequence","fresh-recheck","bridge","core"],"taxonomies":[{"primarySkillCode":"eng.reading.inference","atomicSubskillCode":"eng.reading.inference.attitude-feeling","evidenceFocusCode":"eng.reading.inf